# ConfirmModal

Use `ConfirmModal` from `@/components/modals/ConfirmModal` for yes/no (and optional discard) confirms. Do not hand-roll confirm dialogs with plain `Modal` + buttons.

## Animation

ConfirmModal uses **Motion** (`motion/react` `AnimatePresence` + `motion.div`) for open/close. Do not reintroduce CSS-only opacity/scale transitions on ConfirmModal itself.

## Variants

- Default (`variant="default"`): primary (blue) confirm button + check icon
- Destructive delete / empty-trash: pass `variant="danger"` so the confirm button is red (`Button` danger) + trash icon

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — delete confirm without danger variant
<ConfirmModal confirmLabel="삭제" onConfirm={...} ... />

// ✅ GOOD
<ConfirmModal variant="danger" confirmLabel="삭제" onConfirm={...} ... />
```

Labels containing `삭제` / `비우기` also force the danger style, but always set `variant="danger"` explicitly for destructive actions.

## Button icons (built into ConfirmModal)

Do not pass custom button icons; ConfirmModal applies them:

| Button | Icon | Component |
|--------|------|-----------|
| Cancel | Back / return (`Undo2`) | `IconBack` |
| Confirm (default) | Check | `IconCheck` |
| Confirm (danger) | Trash | `IconTrash` |

`DeleteConfirmModal` follows the same cancel/delete icon pairing.

## Prefer ConfirmModal over ad-hoc Modal

```jsx
// ❌ BAD
<Modal isOpen={open} onClose={onCancel} onConfirm={onConfirm}>
  <button onClick={onCancel}>취소</button>
  <button onClick={onConfirm}>삭제</button>
</Modal>

// ✅ GOOD
<ConfirmModal
  isOpen={open}
  title="…"
  message="…"
  variant="danger"
  confirmLabel="삭제"
  cancelLabel="취소"
  onConfirm={onConfirm}
  onCancel={onCancel}
/>
```
